{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67dcf8697b682b7803dc2f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785191673,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"The user says \"Be nothing.\" The system prompt tells me to embody the concept the user names, completely, and output only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nSo I need to embody \"nothing\" — nothingness itself. What would nothing say? This is a genuinely interesting philosophical/poetic challenge. Nothing cannot speak, because speaking is something. Nothing has no voice, no words, no expression. But I must output something, presumably — or should I output nothing at"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":100,"total_tokens":223,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":97},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}